    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801">

                <pb facs="0792" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00 Statement July 16, 1937/180a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-12T12:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1937—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>373. On Sunday morning next<anchor n="24" xml:id="d801-f1"/> we are publishing a
                    series of comments from governments on the Secretary’s statement of July 16,
                    which was contained in radio bulletin No. 164 of that date.</p>
                <pb facs="0793" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/>
                <p>We have discussed the matter with Ambassador de los Rios, who concurs in our hope
                    that we will be able to include a message of endorsement of these principles
                    from the Spanish Government. To do this it will be necessary for us to receive
                    such a message at the latest by noon Saturday; I fear that if it were published
                    at a later date it would be less effective than if included with the replies of
                    probably 50 other nations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
